Title: RAIN ON MERIDIAN
Author: Walter Kane
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. MERIDIAN AVENUE - RAIN - NIGHT

Neon, wet asphalt. PI FRANK MERCER meets a nervous CLIENT.
CLIENT
My husband keeps late hours. I want names.

INT. MERCER'S OFFICE - DAY

Frank files the retainer. Photos still in the envelope, undeveloped.
FRANK
She's no grieving wife. She's the gray suit's partner — I'd bet the office on it.

INT. MERCER'S OFFICE - NIGHT

Darkroom tray. RED HAT woman enters room 514. Husband follows later.
FRANK
Not infidelity. Timing.

INT. MERIDIAN HOTEL - LOBBY - NIGHT

Desk clerk remembers the husband — checked in, never checked out.

INT. MERIDIAN HOTEL - HALLWAY - NIGHT

Room 415 empty. Matchbook: BLUE PARROT CLUB.

INT. BLUE PARROT CLUB - NIGHT

Green hat and husband swap a METAL CASE under the table.
FRANK
He's not cheating. He's laundering.

EXT. ALLEY BEHIND CLUB - NIGHT

Frank tailing the husband — ambush. A sap to the ribs, darkness.

INT. MERCER'S OFFICE - DAY

Frank bruised, angry. Client on the phone — sweet voice, wrong words.
CLIENT
Did you get the photos I paid for?

INT. MERCER'S OFFICE - NIGHT

Client in person. Envelope on the desk. Rain like nails.
CLIENT
You were supposed to find a cheating husband.

INT. MERCER'S OFFICE - NIGHT

Frank slides the photos back — truth printed on the last frame: the client with the gray suit man.
FRANK
I found a partner. Yours. Hire a worse detective next time.

FADE OUT.


THE END
